{
  "uid": "meizuno-apps",
  "title": "Meizuno — Apps",
  "description": "Per app: requests by route (count, p50/p95, errors), the process's CPU and memory, and CPU/memory profiles by function. Provisioned from git — edit grafana/dashboards/meizuno-apps.json, because the file overrides UI changes on reload.",
  "tags": [
    "meizuno",
    "provisioned"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "browser",
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "app",
        "label": "App",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "victoriametrics"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(python_info, job)",
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(python_info, job)",
          "refId": "app"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "description": "An app with its own /metrics (port 9000). Its Pyroscope service_name is the same name."
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How to read this",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 20,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 1
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "## What this dashboard shows\n\nPick an app above. Everything here comes from the app itself: its own `/metrics` (port 9000, scraped every 30 s) and the profiles it pushes to Pyroscope. Rates are 5-minute averages; the stats and the table cover the whole selected time range.\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Duration** | Measured inside the app, from the request arriving to the **last byte** of the answer. A stream counts whole: English's session stream includes the model writing the exercises, a Forma assistant turn includes the model's reply. Traefik's latency on the overview adds the network in front. |\n| **route** | The declared route template, e.g. `/api/v1/shared/{public_id}/day` — never the real path, which can carry a credential. `static` is the built client's files, `unmatched` is anything no route matched (404s). `/health` is not counted. |\n| **status** | A class: `2xx`, `3xx`, `4xx`, `5xx`. `none` means no response was ever started — an unhandled error on its way to a 500, or a client that left first. |\n| **CPU** | % of **one** core. Limits: english 0.5 core (50%), forma 2 cores (200%). |\n| **Memory** | Resident memory of the Python process. Both apps are limited to 512 MiB; above it the container is OOM-killed. |\n| **instance** | One per container. During `docker rollout` two exist for a moment, so per-instance panels briefly show both. |\n\n## Profiles (bottom row)\n\n- **CPU by function** — where CPU time went, summed over every request in the range. Only time **on** the CPU: a request awaiting Postgres or OpenAI is on no stack while it waits, so \"slow because waiting\" shows in Duration and not here.\n- **Memory allocated by function** — bytes allocated during the range: who churns memory.\n- **Memory in use by function** — sampled heap still held: who keeps memory. A leak grows here.\n- Click a frame to zoom. **Explore → Pyroscope** can diff two time ranges."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Requests in range (count)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(http_request_duration_seconds_count{job=\"$app\"}[$__range]))",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "none",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "description": "Every request except /health, over the selected range."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
